Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?glm-callquote:=20the=20fork=200103=20port=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20a=20call=20quoted=20inside=20prose=20still=20parses?=
 =?UTF-8?q?;=20the=20closer=20scan=20never=20cuts=20a=20call's=20own=20dat?=
 =?UTF-8?q?a=20(zclose=20composes=20first)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

THE PORT: Mia 1104's engine patch 0103, hand-ported against the v1.2.4
+tools256+zclose server state (the composition the image builds: 011-zclose
applies before this patch; both touch only zig/src/server/tool_parse.zig and
its test — order-free against every kernel patch).

Two behaviors, one concern (the call's survival):

1. The envelope's own data (a JSON string value quoting markup, an
   arg_value/parameter region) never ends the call — the zclose port's
   value-aware closer scan. This patch carries it onto the composed base:
   envelopeCloser() tracks JSON string state and arg_value/parameter regions
   across the three envelope scans (the JSON/XML loop, the pipe-spelling loop,
   openCall), falling back to the plain first-tag find when the payload does
   not open as JSON or the JSON never closes outside its strings — a
   malformed payload cuts and is rejected exactly as before.

2. The retry path inside a rejected envelope names an OFFERED tool (the fork's
   kept-list semantics): prose that quotes the opener ahead of a call starts
   the envelope, so the call is the last opener inside it (or one before that,
   when a value quotes the opener too) and the quoting prose stays content; an
   example quoted inside a rejected envelope's cut region stays prose — the
   own-name rule is a whole envelope's rule (010-tools256), not a fragment's.

PROVENANCE: the port is the fork's patch 0103 against the fork's 1.1.9 base,
adapted to our tree's drifted file (the fork's hunks do not apply; the port is
the fork's final file state over our composed base, every fork line accounted
for). The tree this commit produces is byte-identical to the line's v124-rebase
state f202781d3 — the suite-green state (the tool-parse host suite 51/51: the
fork's 0103 suite + the two quoted-markup pins) and compile RC=0 (fatbins +
native, sm_121) are inherited from that state unchanged.

